# This file contains the initial defaults for go command configuration.
# Values set by 'go env -w' and written to the user's go/env file override these.
# The environment overrides everything else.

# Use the Go module mirror and checksum database by default.
# See https://proxy.golang.org for details.
GOPROXY=https://proxy.golang.org,direct
GOSUMDB=sum.golang.org

# Do not download or re-exec another toolchain by default. Upstream ships
# GOTOOLCHAIN=auto here; see https://go.dev/doc/toolchain for what that does.
#
# An official release is linked with PE subsystem 6.1, and Windows XP's loader
# reads that field and refuses the image, so a toolchain fetched by auto
# cannot run on the machine this fork exists for. The failure arrives after
# the download has already succeeded, and is triggered by nothing worse than a
# go.mod asking for a newer version, which any dependency can do.
#
# This is a default, not an enforcement: the environment still overrides it,
# so GOTOOLCHAIN=auto in a shell brings the old behaviour back for anyone who
# means it.
GOTOOLCHAIN=local
